{"game": "mass-effect-andromeda", "language": "english", "appid": 1238000, "month": "2025-10", "window": 4, "start_date": 1761264000, "end_date": 1761955199, "month_true_total": 96, "quota": 5, "returned": 5, "pulled_at": "2026-10-07 22:02:19 UTC", "reviews": [{"recommendationid": "208084975", "author": {"steamid": "76561198111522679", "personaname": "AttackCommander", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/id/AttackCommander/", "num_games_owned": 312, "num_reviews": 16, "playtime_forever": 4265, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 4265, "last_played": 1761891372, "avatar": "e365e45a3a13eebf8a3ddf0315304e499a672cd2"}, "language": "english", "review": "Andromeda is a halfhearted attempt at creating a Mass Effect game. If I had been a longtime fan of the series who bought this at launch after much anticipation, I definitely would be upset. But for a game that is heavily discounted when on sale... a ME newbie like me can look past its flaws.\n\nThe storytelling is clearly lacking in depth and is a rehashing of the reapers from the original trilogy; expect now an unlikely hero trope is used instead (Hollywood would be proud). The voice acting/dialogue and inconsistent facial animations really dash any semblance of seriousness, which is unfortunate.\n\nOverall this game is a nice time sink which keeps the player occupied through repetitive 'missions' in conjunction with the main quest. Graphically there is environmental and planetary eye candy to be had, which is appreciated.", "timestamp_created": 1761949897, "timestamp_updated": 1761949897, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 1, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": "0.509803950786590576", "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1591887420", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "208084024", "author": {"steamid": "76561198298572396", 